				<r3d:description language="eng">SIP-Archiv is an Internet based archive and database for petrophysical data derived by Spectral Induced Polarization (SIP) measurements on sediments and consolidated rocks, building materials, man-made materials and wood. It is open for all SIP related working Groups, and the usage is free of charge for scientific purposes. Nevertheless, a simple registration is needed for both, the users and the user&#039;s institution. More details can be found on the website.</r3d:description>
